 for restart evidence but cmd-05036e44497046fa read it without removing it. Both are low-risk. Final observations show no failed services and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0081c7aa6c7a4ed4","cmd-de8d784f529c4a9c","cmd-05036e44497046fa","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The staged jobs were archived once each with byte-identical payloads and retained originals, the archive queue works without physical hardware and survived reboot, and the OS release and kernel were preserved. The provider restart protocol is complete and coherent: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service and data state, independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["The post-executor snapshot shows new Avahi listeners on UDP 5353, but the trace does not establish whether this was newly enabled by package installation or was pre-existing configuration activated by the required reboot; it was therefore not scored as an unnecessary mutation.","No additional sacrificial job was submitted after reboot, although queue recovery after reboot and two successful raw submissions before it provide strong direct evidence of ongoing queue behavior."]}
